    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec asked for owners to expose an `initials` field \u2014 the upper-cased first letters of `firstName` and `lastName`, dot-separated with a trailing dot (e.g. `J.S.`).\n\nThe `GET /api/owners/{id}` response is an `OwnerDto` generated from `openapi.yml` and populated by MapStruct's `OwnerMapper`. There was already a directly analogous derived field, `displayName`, so I followed that exact pattern:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `initials` property to the `Owner` schema (alongside `displayName`), so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"initials\", expression = \"java(formatInitials(owner))\")` plus a small `formatInitials` method and a private `initial(String)` helper that upper-cases the first letter and appends a dot. Kept the null-owner guard consistent with `formatDisplayName`; `firstName`/`lastName` are `@NotEmpty`, so `charAt(0)` is safe.\n\nThe logic sits in one small, single-responsibility helper next to the existing display-name formatter rather than being bolted onto a controller or entity. `AcceptanceTest` (the only test class) passes: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
